Now JS. Replace camera FOV line and control/animation block.

Line 24: `new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(54,innerWidth/innerHeight,.1,220)` -> 66 and rotation order.

Need note isMobile defined after startGame but startGame uses isMobile; function called after definition of const isMobile? Actually startGame function defined line 66 and isMobile defined line 67, start button listener line 66. By click time isMobile initialized. Fine. But I'll restructure maybe.

Let's replace lines 66-69 entirely with new controls:

```
let yaw=0,camPitch=.02,keys={},started=false,walk=0,joy={x:0,y:0},toastTimer;
const welcome=document.querySelector('#welcome');
const isMobile=matchMedia('(max-width:700px)').matches;
function startGame(){if(started)return;started=true;document.body.classList.add('playing');welcome.classList.add('gone');const hint=document.querySelector('#hint');hint.style.opacity=1;setTimeout(()=>hint.style.opacity=0,isMobile?5500:8000)}
document.querySelector('#start').addEventListener('click',startGame);

// mouse / touch-drag look on the scene
let dragging=false,lastX=0,lastY=0;
function lookBy(dx,dy,s=1){yaw-=dx*.004*s;camPitch=THREE.MathUtils.clamp(camPitch-dy*.0028*s,-1.15,1.15)}
renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerdown',e=>{if(!started)return;dragging=true;lastX=e.clientX;lastY=e.clientY;renderer.domElement.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId)});
renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerup',()=>dragging=false);
renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{if(!dragging||!started)return;lookBy(e.clientX-lastX,e.clientY-lastY);lastX=e.clientX;lastY=e.clientY});
addEventListener('keydown',...same...); addEventListener('keyup',...)
const touch..., stick..., lookPad=document.querySelector('#look'), lookStick=document.querySelector('.look-stick');
let touchId=null;
function setStick(el,x,y){el.style.transform=`translate(${x}px,${y}px)`}
...
```

Need joystick coordinates max based on radius. Pad 126, stick 50, center offset 38. Max = 38-ish. Current max 41. We'll use 38. Function:
```
function padVector(e,pad){let r=pad.getBoundingClientRect(); return {x:e.clientX-(r.left+r.width/2), y:e.clientY-(r.top+r.height/2)}}
function clampPad(dx,dy,max=38){let len=Math.hypot(dx,dy); if(len>max){dx*=max/len;dy*=max/len} return {x:dx,y:dy}}
```
Joystick move sets joy = {x:dx/38,y:dy/38} and transform.

Look pad: yaw/pitch updated based on delta from last look position:
```
let lookId=null,lookX=0,lookY=0;
lookPad.addEventListener('pointerdown',e=>{e.preventDefault();lookId=e.pointerId;lookPad.setPointerCapture(lookId);lookPad.classList.add('active');startGame();lookX=e.clientX;lookY=e.clientY});
lookPad.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{if(e.pointerId!==lookId)return;lookBy(e.clientX-lookX,e.clientY-lookY,1.25);lookX=e.clientX;lookY=e.clientY;let {x,y}=clampPad((e.clientX-lookX)*0, ...)});
```
Wait knob offset should reflect touch offset within pad, not delta. Show a small shift: use vector from center clamped ~26. On pointerdown set lookStick transform accordingly, on move too? If finger returns to center while still dragging, knob follow position. That gives visual. But delta look tracking independent. On release reset.

```
function moveLook(e){let r=lookPad.getBoundingClientRect(),dx=e.clientX-(r.left+r.width/2),dy=e.clientY-(r.top+r.height/2);let c=clampPad(dx,dy,26);setStick(lookStick,c.x,c.y)}
```
lookStick has css left 38 top 38; transform moves.

On pointerup reset transform.

Touch joystick currently `pointerdown` calls startGame which hides welcome; but welcome overlay covers screen so pads not clickable before start; start button starts. Fine.

On canvas pointerdown before started return. But welcome covers with pointer-events auto. Good.

Need hide hint desktop only? We'll set timeout all.

Now animate block. Replace lines 71-78.

New:
```
const clock=new THREE.Clock();const EYE={height:1.79,forward:.27};camera.rotation.order='YXZ';
function animate(){requestAnimationFrame(animate);let dt=Math.min(clock.getDelta(),.04),t=clock.elapsedTime;
 let forward=...,side=...; let mag=...
 if(started&&moving){
   ...
   const speed=4.7,sin=Math.sin(yaw),cos=Math.cos(yaw);
   let dx=(-sin*forward+cos*side)*speed*dt,dz=(-cos*forward-sin*side)*speed*dt;
   ...
   walk+=dt*10;
   ...
 } else {...}
 avatar.rotation.y=yaw+Math.PI;
 const bob=moving?Math.abs(Math.sin(walk*2))*.05:Math.sin(t*1.7)*.012;
 avatar.position.y=moving?bob*.7:0; // body subtle
 camera.position.set(player.position.x-Math.sin(yaw)*EYE.forward, EYE.height+bob, player.position.z-Math.cos(yaw)*EYE.forward);
 camera.rotation.set(camPitch,yaw,0);
 ...
 cards...
 renderer.render...
}
```
Note camera.rotation.set(x,y,z) preserves order YXZ. Good.

Card collection triggers based on player position.

One issue: camera position y doesn't include player.position.y (always 0). Fine.

Start position 0,0,8.5 is on central avenue facing? yaw=0 looks -z toward fountain at 0,0, so nice.

When looking down at feet, body visible? Fine.

Update CSS `body.playing` class added; crosshair appears.

Pointer lock? Not required. But desktop "mouse to look" suggests move mouse without dragging, which we don't implement. Hint says mouse or drag. look-note says "move mouse to look" inaccurate. Change to "drag to look" or implement pointer lock. Current control drag-to-look is fine. I changed look-note to "move mouse to look" — not accurate. Either implement pointer lock or revert. Could implement click-to-lock? Might complicate UI. Better use "drag to look" to match. Update later.

Actually maybe desktop first-person could use pointer lock on click after start: standard. But drag works. Keep drag.

